comments[42]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-16T15:14:51.889Z",codex-gpt5-root,"PR #573 CI evidence: static quality, package boundary, and all token-budget measurements passed, but final rmSync of /tmp/pm-token-budget-AclN4M hit transient ENOTEMPTY. The same gate passed locally before and after the run; this confirms the existing broader temp-lifecycle chore still owns cleanup retry/signal hardening. No script implementation was added in this review slice because the next PR head naturally reruns the full gate and this item's acceptance criteria also require compile-cache plus every mkdtemp caller, not a one-line partial close."
  "2026-07-21T06:54:35.054Z",codex-root-20260721,"Live GitHub evidence 2026-07-21: Auto Release run 29804774154 / GH-626 failed after all coverage measurements when scripts/release/token-budget-gate.mjs final rmSync hit ENOTEMPTY on /tmp/pm-token-budget-fyfySy under Node 24. Reusing this canonical temp-lifecycle item; no duplicate created."
  "2026-07-21T07:33:06.446Z",codex-root-20260721,"Progress evidence: fixed Auto Release GH-626 by routing token-budget cleanup through the shared resilient retry primitive; consolidated external-package and contracts cleanup; added version-scoped compile-cache generation pruning. Broader every-mkdtemp signal cleanup remains, so this item stays open and is released after this PR slice."
  "2026-07-21T07:39:45.232Z",codex-root-20260721,"Verification evidence: both linked cleanup runs now pass (15 token-budget cleanup tests; 26 compile-cache/shared-cleanup tests across four suites)."
  "2026-07-21T07:45:23.196Z",codex-root-20260721,"Full-suite correction: removed the unnecessary existsSync postcondition from cleanupTempRoot so force-recursive deletion remains compatible with partial fs mocks while retaining outer retry/sweep behavior; synthesized non-Error failures now preserve the original value. All 37 cleanup/script tests pass."
  "2026-07-21T07:54:57.149Z",codex-root-20260721,"Final verification: the public compile-cache generation resolver is directly covered alongside pruning and resilient cleanup; the complete 6045-test coverage suite passes at exactly 100% lines/statements/functions/branches. This PR intentionally leaves the broader every-mkdtemp signal-handler acceptance work open."
  "2026-07-21T08:12:07.571Z",codex-root-20260721,"Greptile remediation: compile-cache pruning now reads string directory entries directly instead of allocating Dirent objects only to discard their type metadata. Focused lifecycle coverage remains green."
  "2026-07-21T08:16:41.647Z",codex-root-20260721,"Final review-head proof: the allocation simplification and resilient cleanup path pass the complete 6052-test suite at exact 100% coverage."
  "2026-07-21T09:10:30.997Z",codex-root-20260721,"Hosted review remediation: compile-cache generation names now reject unsafe filename tokens and pruning retains a bounded fresh-concurrency grace so two pm versions starting together cannot delete one another. A real filesystem race test removes a candidate between readdir and stat; only ENOENT is ignored and all other failures remain visible."
  "2026-07-21T09:15:16.813Z",codex-root-20260721,"Exact remediation-head proof: all 332 test files and 6053 tests pass at 100/100/100/100 coverage. This PR completes bounded, concurrency-safe compile-cache generations and resilient cleanup surfaces, while the remaining every-mkdtemp signal-handler work stays open in this same canonical item."
  "2026-07-21T10:13:36.637Z",codex-root-20260721,"Hosted CI remediation: Windows Node 24 exhausted the prior 375 ms helper retry window with EBUSY on the generated workspace. Test sandboxes now apply Node's recursive rm retry contract plus the same eight-attempt 120 ms backoff used by production cleanup."
  "2026-07-21T10:14:17.179Z",codex-root-20260721,"Hosted CodeRabbit remediation: compile-cache validation now accepts leading underscore and hyphen safe tokens, matching resolveCompileCacheGeneration for scoped package names such as @org/package while continuing to reject dot segments and path separators. Focused SDK and scale-workspace suites pass (10 tests)."
  "2026-07-21T10:29:28.119Z",codex-root-20260721,"Exact final-head proof: 332 test files and 6053 tests pass; compile-cache scoped-package generation and Windows-portable cleanup are covered within 100% statements (40688/40688), branches (28623/28623), functions (8264/8264), and lines (39582/39582)."
  "2026-07-21T10:31:05.390Z",codex-root-20260721,"Installed-package acceptance proof: pnpm smoke:npx packed the current tree, installed it into a fresh temporary project, exercised the CLI and all 13 bundled packages, and cleaned the sandbox successfully (version 2026.7.21)."
  "2026-07-21T10:47:25.985Z",codex-root-20260721,"Final exact-commit Greptile review scored 5/5 with no comments, but noted a soft resolver/validator contract gap for empty or leading-dot inputs. Tightening the public resolver invariant before push."
  "2026-07-21T10:52:29.795Z",codex-root-20260721,"Greptile contract remediation verified: resolver now trims empty versions to development and rewrites a leading dot, so every generated token is accepted by pruning; scoped, empty, dot-prefixed, and traversal-shaped cases are covered. Full 6053-test suite remains exact 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-07-22T19:18:04.059Z",codex-sdk-boundary-20260722,"GitHub provenance: GH-626 now contains a direct system-of-record link to this canonical release temp/cache cleanup lineage; the GitHub issue is closed while this broader pm follow-up remains open."
  "2026-08-09T16:21:33.779Z","harness:codex","Fresh reproduction 2026-08-09 after PR #952: the published 2026.8.9 installed-agent verifier completed all 10 lifecycle steps under both npm and Bun with ok:true, then the verifier process exited nonzero because final recursive cleanup hit ENOTEMPTY on its temporary root. Reusing this broader open item rather than creating a duplicate; the result proves acceptance behavior is healthy while cleanup can still mask success."
  "2026-09-18T23:35:36.587Z","harness:codex","Current-tranche reproduction: the default temporary filesystem user quota refused writes during npm tarball extraction and interrupted broad coverage setup. An external scratch root with no initialized tracker in its ancestors restores isolation; a home-relative external root still discovers the home tracker in tests that intentionally unset PM_PATH, as already documented in the Sep 8 note. No unrelated temporary artifacts were deleted. This remains the canonical footprint/cleanup follow-up; no duplicate created."
  "2026-09-21T09:55:08.917Z","harness:codex","Current implementation scope: shared process-owned sandbox lifecycle and adoption by package smoke, dogfood, contract snapshot, plugin MCP harness and sandboxed test runner. Existing compile-cache generation pruning remains in place. Signal cleanup must stop registered children before deleting their workspace, preserve explicit keep-temp requests, and unregister normal-completion resources. SIGKILL cannot run cleanup; do not claim that guarantee."
  "2026-09-21T10:06:14.090Z","harness:codex","Verification: 86 focused tests passed across lease ownership, cleanup, package smoke, contract snapshots and plugin MCP harness. Both new or changed lifecycle primitives separately meet exact 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines (73 statements, 40 branches, 9 functions, 67 lines). Real subprocess tests prove normal exit, uncaught failure, explicit retention and Unix interrupts. Adoption currently covers five primary smoke and contract entrypoints; test-runner and other release/benchmark scripts remain pending under this broader canonical item."
  "2026-09-21T10:14:51.540Z","harness:codex","Full-suite attempt: 9167 tests passed and three existing scale/refusal tests timed out under concurrent local validation load; no valid full coverage report was produced. Preserving all thresholds and timeout contracts; rerun with reduced worker concurrency after other gates finish. Packed npm/npx/bunx smoke and package-first dogfood passed; published 2026.9.21 npm/Bun installed-agent lifecycle and npx/bunx MCP stdio/HTTP verification also passed."
  "2026-09-21T10:23:21.468Z","harness:codex","Final changed-script coverage: 132 tests across seven suites passed at exact 786/786 statements, 392/392 branches, 113/113 functions and 761/761 lines. Both plugin MCP smoke workflows passed. An independent temporary-directory manual run exercised CLI init/create/claim/update/comments/notes/learnings/close/release/validate and confirmed complete closed-state reads through the public PmClient SDK. Linked test executions are recorded by pm test; remaining runner migration remains explicitly open."
  "2026-09-21T10:42:39.361Z","harness:codex","PR 1283 review: accepting CodeRabbit finding 4061327789. Exit-time console output can be buffered on piped stderr, so retained-workspace diagnostics will use best-effort synchronous writes while preserving the original failure if stderr is unavailable. Add observable output and closed-stderr regressions. First hosted round settled with 37 successful, one neutral and two skipped checks; Sourcery reported review quota exhaustion."
  "2026-09-21T10:50:33.971Z","harness:codex","Completed five-entrypoint delivery is now represented by child pm-14dnbh so package-generated release notes include the shipped behavior. This parent remains open and unclaimed for the explicitly inventoried runner, benchmark and release-script migration."
  "2026-09-22T09:47:52.735Z","harness:codex","Implementation delivery is split into child pm-xjy565 for eleven named entrypoints, with behavioral installer-exit and runner-signal regressions. Remaining producer-specific work: packed-first-run, run-scale-benchmarks, cli-transport-floor, docs-skills-gate, agent-task-token-gate and token-budget-gate. Those asynchronous or coupled lifecycles require separate shutdown review; this parent is not being closed as complete."
  "2026-10-04T09:26:02.730Z","harness:codex","Fresh recurrence during PR #1387 validation: temporary user quota interrupted packing, full-suite fixture creation and lock-owner publication while filesystem-wide free bytes remained. Disk-backed scratch outside tracker ancestry allowed the source suite to run. To retain the original token-accounting path width, one generated test fixture from this run was relocated reversibly to disk, all 10014 file SHA-256 values were checked before/after and its original path retained as a symlink; the unchanged nine-task token gate then passed. No unrelated temporary data, quota, gate limit or host service was changed. Broader producer cleanup and footprint acceptance remains open/unclaimed; these observations do not close the umbrella."
  "2026-10-07T17:18:42.682Z","harness:codex","Active final adoption work: review the six residual release/benchmark roots plus newer package-distribution and reliability collector roots. Also investigate GH-1423 detached telemetry root resurrection at the producer boundary. Full all-status corpus, predecessor metadata and full histories captured with no omissions; completed fixture-specific pm-idj82e stays closed. Only this lifecycle owner and pm-gh1424 are in progress."
  "2026-10-07T17:31:02.720Z","harness:codex","Regression evidence: three public telemetry flush tests failed on the unmodified implementation because a removed installation was recreated both before worker startup and during successful/failed HTTP delivery. The new storage-parent policy is additive in the SDK; detached workers opt out of settings scaffolding and parent creation for queue locks, atomic rewrites and state persistence. Existing consent, concurrency and runtime suites remain green. A missing coordination parent must fail promptly rather than consume the contention wait budget."
  "2026-10-07T17:41:36.655Z","harness:codex","All-status graph baseline: strict complete census of 2902 items and 14857 deduplicated directed edges, including 2606 terminal nodes; zero missing references, isolates, sparse active nodes, hierarchy/ordering cycles, stale lifecycle blockers or ordering contradictions. Every active and terminal subject reaches a declared outcome through the typed traversal policy. Two information-only findings retain historical hierarchy aliases across seven subjects; these are not rewritten into invented ancestry. Current cleanup closure adds evidence-derived lineage through the existing parent and closed producer-lifecycle deliveries."
  "2026-10-07T17:53:48.860Z","harness:codex","Packed acceptance: one local 2026.10.7 tarball installed through npm and Bun in isolated temporary projects. Both completed init/create/claim/comments/notes/learnings/files/context/close/release/history validation; npx and bunx resolved the local installed CLI. Public SDK complete-list, concurrent merge install, and parent-preserving storage writes passed. Real telemetry flush worker binaries under Node and Bun each delivered two captured start/finish events after the collector removed the root; neither in-flight completion nor absent-root startup recreated it. This proves the local artifact, not a new registry publication."
  "2026-10-07T17:58:18.915Z","harness:codex","Interrupt acceptance: an actual cli-transport-floor entrypoint ran under an isolated TMPDIR. A filesystem event detected its persisted settings during fixture seeding and SIGTERM was delivered. The process exited 143, left zero owned pm-cli-cold-floor roots, and preserved an unrelated sentinel. No polling or unrelated cleanup was used. Security secret scan (including tracked PM history) and documentation links passed. GitHub Dependabot, code-scanning and secret-scanning open alert counts remain zero."
  "2026-10-07T18:00:53.054Z","harness:codex","Full-suite first pass: 9889 tests passed; three failures were the new root SDK test crossing the 120-file directory cap, stale SDK signatures after additive storage options, and Homebrew npm/package.json lookup. The new test moves into tests/unit/sdk/storage; the official snapshot generator records compatibility reasoning. The next run exposes the actual npm global module directory via NODE_PATH. No directory cap, coverage denominator, timeout, test assertion, or security threshold is relaxed. Consolidated the five overlapping linked-test entries into one union so token-budget and lifecycle suites execute once per linked verification."
  "2026-10-07T18:13:37.017Z","harness:codex","Organization rationale: the storage policy regression lives in tests/unit/sdk/storage so it does not expand the full SDK root directory. The remaining global domain-folder program remains the canonical pm-kb5h scope; this narrow addition neither implements nor closes that broader program. New files use existing merge/telemetry/release domains and the SDK storage lifecycle doc is reachable from docs/README. Full live history-drift validation checked 2903 items with zero drift; its 170 legacy structured-resolution warnings remain historical evidence gaps, not invented outcomes."
  "2026-10-07T18:52:22.915Z","harness:codex","Fresh graph audit before closeout: 2904 items and 14871 deduplicated directed edges across ten kinds; all active and terminal items reach their outcome anchors, with no missing references, sparse/isolated items, ordering or hierarchy cycles, stale lifecycle blockers, or ordering contradictions. Seven preserved legacy subjects have informational hierarchy storage/cardinality findings. This delivery adds implements, verifies and discovered_from lineage for the new issues; it does not invent historical ancestry or bulk-add weak related links."
  "2026-10-07T18:55:22.858Z","harness:codex","Required production Sentry/telemetry gate passed on 2026-10-07: authenticated 14-day Sentry query has zero critical/high/unresolved faults; seven-day weighted finish error rate is 3.19% against 6%, with zero missing error-code rows. Telemetry API, ingestion worker, Postgres, RabbitMQ and Tempo are healthy; queue is empty, one consumer is present, and 101995 events arrived in the preceding 24 hours. Production service remains version 2026.10.4 and published CLI 2026.10.7; neither is evidence that this branch is deployed. Earlier live context probe produced fresh start/finish events. The one-hour Sentry trace query is empty, so trace freshness is not certified."
  "2026-10-07T19:08:17.235Z","harness:codex","Full-source final attempt preserved as failed: 9896 cases passed, one existing composed-continuation context case returned one row where 26 were expected. Coverage nevertheless reached exact integer 100/100/100/100 (lines64023/64023, statements67190/67190, functions13853/13853, branches51419/51419). No uncovered code remains. The first isolated rerun traversed all source cursor scenarios successfully before exposing the omitted Homebrew NODE_PATH prerequisite at npm packing; rerunning with the same verified npm discovery used by full coverage. No assertion, token ceiling, retry count or gate was loosened; the original cause is not established."
  "2026-10-07T19:10:59.116Z","harness:codex","The unchanged composed-continuation integration now passes in isolation with verified Homebrew npm discovery, including all list/search/context serialized-cursor journeys and actual packed Node/Bun public SDK consumers. All three final linked receipts are passed: lifecycle union280cases/20files (test-local-muyhailm-vngabk), Git merge27cases/2files (test-local-muyhbmgq-mv5h70), custom-field267cases/4files (test-local-muyhc350-xmcq8a). The earlier whole attempt remains failed; only a new fully passing whole run can certify full-suite acceptance. Exact coverage arithmetic already passed without exclusions or denominator changes beyond inlining a previously covered one-call helper."
  "2026-10-07T19:28:14.715Z","harness:codex","Artifact negative control: the actual physical publication gate rejects source distribution20005879 bytes above the unchanged20000000 ceiling. All maintained runtime/type/public-manifest paths must remain; no budget/profile relaxation is allowed. Fully inspected the three overlapping build, first-run and lifecycle pages. Consolidate their shared ownership prose and route detailed boundaries through focused links while retaining lease timing, producer shutdown, consumer/control separation, README parsing and registry/telemetry claims. This also removes the obsolete statement that final producer migration is still pending."
  "2026-10-07T19:33:59.918Z","harness:codex","Added bounded semantic failure diagnostics to the existing composed-continuation assertion: command, delivered IDs and both cursor-transition counts are retained if it fails again. Expected row count26/30 remains unchanged, and no test is added or retried automatically. Consolidated public acceptance docs now share explicit ownership links; the real artifact gate passes at19999737 source bytes before the final additional prose reduction and reviewed changelog generation. Runtime bundle limits remain separately enforced."
  "2026-10-07T19:35:30.072Z","harness:codex","Final installed-artifact manual acceptance passed for physical distribution a3cddbf03fed5f964099a8b41b8396ddfa746f19: 6489files/43333966unpacked bytes with the tested40-package runtime closure; source distribution19999082<20000000, runtime23334884<25000000 and4731<5000files. npm/npx and Bun/bunx each complete isolated CLI init/create/claim/annotations/evidence/context/close/release/validation plus SDK strict-complete reads, three concurrent merge installs and existing-parent storage policy. Each actual installed telemetry worker delivers two events after loopback collector removal and preserves absent-root startup. Rejected-field JSON/human recovery preserves item/history bytes. Documentation consolidation reduces the three acceptance pages by6797bytes while retaining shared ownership/limits; reviewed changelog remains pending."
  "2026-10-07T19:53:30.335Z","harness:codex","Final local acceptance before reviewed delivery: full sandboxed coverage passed 9,897 tests (787 passed files; platform-only skips preserved), with exact lines 64,023/64,023, statements 67,190/67,190, functions 13,853/13,853 and branches 51,419/51,419. All owner-linked checks passed, including the existing packed continuation regression under real npm/npx and Bun/bunx. Actual bundled shipping-artifact acceptance passed isolated CLI/SDK workflows, concurrent real Git setup, rejected custom-field immutability and telemetry completion after owned-root deletion. Dependency audit and tracked-file secret scan found zero findings. Strict static prefix passed; the unchanged Node 24 import admission and remaining assurance/mutation gates passed separately. The retained aggregate Node 26 timing failure and earlier failed coverage attempts remain failed receipts, not reported as passes. Full live history verification matched item hashes. Closure records local source acceptance; hosted review, merge and the next eligible immutable daily publication remain distinct."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-08T06:09:36.684Z","harness:codex","Temporary storage observation 2026-09-08: the host default temporary filesystem reached its 1,048,576-inode limit while still showing free bytes. Tests honoring an external tmpdir could proceed, but hard-coded /tmp fixtures still failed. The current isolation repair pm-bukwmy switches the affected vector, SDK exemplar and MCP Skills fixtures to owned tmpdir roots and preserves cleanup. No unrelated temporary files were deleted. A scratch directory beneath another initialized tracker can still affect ancestor-discovery tests even when outside this checkout; document that boundary and keep long-term temporary footprint/cleanup and runner isolation as separate acceptance scopes."
  "2026-09-21T10:17:53.904Z","harness:codex","Remaining lifecycle adoption inventory after this delivery: scripts/run-tests.mjs; bench/point-read-costs, context-read-costs, run-scale-benchmarks and cli-transport-floor; release/verify-published-release, verify-installed-agent-session, docs-skills-gate, packed-first-run, context-eval-gate, isolated-regression-control, run-release-pipeline, agent-task-token-gate, refusal-closure-gate, token-budget-gate, context-intent-calibration-gate and compatibility-check (all .mjs under scripts). Review each full producer/consumer lifecycle before registration; async children require bounded stop-before-delete callbacks. Existing finally cleanup is not proof of interrupt cleanup. SIGKILL, power loss and forced Windows process termination cannot execute process cleanup handlers."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T17:58:19.647Z","harness:codex","A finally block alone cannot clean an interrupted process. Register synchronous producers for exit/signal cleanup; asynchronous producers must close stage admission, stop or await consumers, and only then delete owned roots. Bounded unfinished shutdown retains evidence; SIGKILL and power loss cannot run handlers. Detached telemetry must also respect storage removal at every write and lock boundary, not just at startup."
